Release the reference of the Ro timer that fired when ims_charging kills a call.

Every Ro timer holds a reference on its session: dlg_callback_received()
takes one when it starts the timer, and resume_ro_session_ontimeout() takes
one for the timer it puts back and releases the one of the timer that fired.
A call killed for lack of credit is the case where no timer is put back:
ro_session_ontimeout() (the reservation ran out) and the "no more credit"
branch of resume_ro_session_ontimeout() both end the call and leave the
fired timer's reference taken. dlg_terminated() cannot release it, because
remove_ro_timer() finds the timer already off the list (the "inconsistent
ro timer data" warning) and so it releases the dialog's reference only.

The session therefore never reached a reference count of 0: it stayed in
the table, active_ro_sessions kept counting it after the dialog was gone
and the memory was never freed. One session per killed call, seen as 10
left over from 10 calls killed after their 20 s of credit.

The "no more credit" branch of resume_ro_session_ontimeout() skips the
release the other branches make at its end, because call_terminated is set,
so release it right after the kill. Both releases come while the reference is
still held, so the session cannot go away under them.

diff --git a/src/modules/ims_charging/ro_timer.c b/src/modules/ims_charging/ro_timer.c
index e7a5496aa5..0944e9a394 100644
--- a/src/modules/ims_charging/ro_timer.c
+++ b/src/modules/ims_charging/ro_timer.c
@@ -388,6 +388,10 @@ void resume_ro_session_ontimeout(
 			ro_session_unlock(ro_session_table, ro_session_entry);
 
 			ro_kill_call(i_req->ro_session, NULL);
+			/* the timer that fired is not put back, so its reference is
+			 * ours to release: dlg_terminated() finds no timer to remove
+			 * and only releases the dialog's own */
+			unref_ro_session(i_req->ro_session, 1, 1);
 			call_terminated = 1;
 		} else {
 			LM_DBG("No more credit for user - letting call run out of money in "
@@ -549,5 +553,9 @@ void ro_session_ontimeout(struct ro_tl *tl)
 	}
 
 	ro_kill_call(ro_session, &default_out_of_credit_hdrs);
+	/* the timer that fired is not put back, so its reference is ours to
+	 * release: dlg_terminated() finds no timer to remove and only releases
+	 * the dialog's own */
+	unref_ro_session(ro_session, 1, 1);
 	return;
 }
